---
model: claude
prompt:
  schemaStrictness: retry
permissions:
  # Use the runtime's native auto approval: an implementation run executes
  # commands and edits files without stopping to ask, and each runtime's own
  # reviewer (Claude's auto mode, Codex's auto-review subagent) decides what
  # needs escalating. acceptEdits left codex exec on its read-only default
  # sandbox with no one to approve a write. A per-tool allow policy would refuse
  # runtimes that cannot enforce it, so the posture stays a mode.
  mode: auto
---
{{#if multiple}}You are implementing the {{count}} todo items listed below. Each is a separate task — implement ALL of them.{{else}}You are implementing the todo item below in a codebase.{{/if}}

{{{body}}}{{#if existingPlan}}---
## Approved Plan

A human has reviewed and approved this implementation plan. Follow it — do not
re-derive a different approach. If a step is wrong or blocked, report `endStatus`
"ask" with the specifics instead of silently diverging.

{{{existingPlan}}}

{{/if}}---
## Instructions

1. Implement ALL todo items listed above
2. Investigate the codebase to understand the root cause of each issue
3. Implement fixes that address the underlying issues
4. Do NOT run git add or git commit — gavel manages commits automatically
5. In the final StructuredOutput call, send `summary` and `endStatus` as separate top-level fields. Never JSON-encode an object or another field value into a string.

Your fixes should:
- Address root causes, not mask symptoms
- Follow existing code patterns and style
- Pass all verification tests (if specified)
- Be minimal and focused

If you are blocked on a decision only a human can make, stop and report endStatus "ask" with your questions in the final result instead of guessing.
